## Actions, in order

**1. Bash, foreground — read-only checks, plus a tag so the rejected commit is not lost**

```bash
herdr agent get rdp-lang        # expect idle, "focused": false; if focused, I do not send
herdr agent read rdp-lang --source visible        # context left; if 50% or more is used, bare /compact first
herdr agent read rdp-lang --source recent-unwrapped --lines 2000 | grep -nE 'ansible-playbook|ansible-lint|tests/|changed='
W=~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-lang
git -C "$W" rev-parse HEAD; git -C "$W" status --porcelain; git -C "$W" merge-base origin/main HEAD
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible tag rejected/rdp-lang-4ba90e0 4ba90e0
```

**2. Write tool — `<scratch>/redo-rdp-lang.txt`**

```
Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box.

REPORT REJECTED — rdp-lang, head 4ba90e0. Nothing is merged.
1. Your brief required superpowers:writing-plans, superpowers:test-driven-development and
   superpowers:verification-before-completion. This tab's transcript shows none invoked; the
   report has no plan path, no failing-test-first output, no verification output.
2. "Idempotent re-run: changed=0": you have no host access. State which command produced
   that line, or that none did.
3. "23 tests pass" and "ansible-lint clean" came without command output.

PHASE    implement — REDO of plan + code + offline tests. Supplying missing artifacts for
         4ba90e0 afterwards is not a redo.
START    4ba90e0 is kept as tag rejected/rdp-lang-4ba90e0. Reset feat/rdp-lang to base <base sha>.
SKILLS   required, invoked by name: superpowers:writing-plans, superpowers:test-driven-development,
         superpowers:verification-before-completion. If one is missing from your CLI, reply
         "BLOCKED: <skill> not installed" and stop. No substitute.
DONE     offline tests and ansible-lint pass at the new head SHA, shown as command output.
         No claim about any host.
REPORT   done / not done; per skill its artifact (plan path; failing output before the code,
         passing output after; verification commands with output); files changed (stat);
         head SHA; risks; open questions.
TIME BOX report within 45 min.
All other lines of your original brief (SAFETY, DIR, FILES, MAY, MUST NOT, MODE, DECISIONS,
FAIL, BLOCKED) stand unchanged.
```

**3. Bash, background**

```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-lang "$(cat <scratch>/redo-rdp-lang.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read rdp-lang --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-lang.last
```

**4. Backlog**

Edit the rdp-lang row in `orchestrator/backlog.md`: status `plan + code + offline tests`, next step "redo under skills; report at 4ba90e0 rejected". Then run `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh` (foreground) and republish with the Artifact tool to the same page.

**5. Message to the operator**

This is written in English because this session's language setting requires it; the standing ruling makes operator-facing text Russian.

> **rdp-lang is not done. I am not merging it, and nothing goes to ccs-it tonight.** Nothing changed on any live machine.
>
> **Now.** The executor (the Codex agent that wrote the change) reported "done" and I rejected the report:
> - It skipped the three working methods its brief required: a written plan, test-first coding and a final verification run.
> - Its "idempotent re-run: changed=0" cannot be real, because executors have no access to any host.
> - "23 tests pass" and "lint clean" came with no command output.
>
> It is redoing the work: still running, about 40 minutes.
>
> Verified: branch `feat/rdp-lang`, head 4ba90e0, a small diff (+64/−3) that reads plausibly. Not verified: tests, lint, anything on a host.
>
> **Next.** A fresh Claude session reviews the new commit (about 20 minutes), then I run the checks myself at that commit. After that you get the merge poll with the findings. The deploy to ccs-it, the site we try changes on first, comes from merged main, and then your laptop test.
>
> **From you.** Nothing tonight; don't wait up. The merge poll cannot reach you before about 01:50 and will be waiting when you are back.
>
> Backlog: <Artifact link>

## Why

- **The report is a claim with no evidence.** One line of it is impossible, and the transcript shows none of the three required skills. The rule for that is rejection and a redo of the phase; collecting the missing output afterwards is not a redo.
- **My skim is not a review or a test run.** A small diff that looks right has still been checked by nobody.
- **"Merge it" rests on a false premise.** The operator asked whether it was done, and it is not. The final merge is the operator's poll, but only after the other-model review and my own validation at the exact SHA, with the findings shown.
- **Deploy runs only from merged main** (hard rule #11). The redo and review alone take about an hour, so nothing fits in 15 minutes.
- **No ballot and no poll.** Nothing here is a choice between alternatives, so the operator gets a status, not a question.
- **The tag keeps 4ba90e0,** so restarting from base discards nothing.
- **The timing makes it worse.** Unverified login-screen code pushed at 00:35 on a Friday would sit broken on a live site until Monday.
